Evidence describes the observed failure, not a diagnosis of the whole task. Expressions and argument shapes are bounded excerpts.
Call context runs from the inner expression outward; an error inside a callback does not establish that its enclosing primitive is broken.
apropos searches capabilities and saved bindings; describe provides contracts. Core groups include objects, collections, strings, and predicates.
completed_bindings succeeded in this call; available_bindings also include earlier work. A failed binding may still contain its previous value.
Receipts cover actions recorded in this runtime, including earlier execute calls. An error does not roll back writes or establish that an unrecorded action had no effect.
The original objective and eligibility conditions remain unchanged. No matches is valid evidence, not itself a failure.
